@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] client-confines-credentials
RPC and first-party usage requests MUST use fixed API paths under the configured
server, with no userinfo, query or fragment in its base URL. Native transports MUST
NOT follow redirects. Credentials and sign-in payloads MUST use HTTPS except for
the existing localhost, 127.0.0.1 and 10.0.2.2 development hosts. Errors and timing
events MUST NOT include request arguments or credential values. Source: root
`phone-api-one-account`, `data-no-user-credentials` and the accepted 21 Oct 2026
iOS client boundary; Devin Review on PR 58.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] client-invalidates-old-sources
Native adapters MUST advance the configuration generation on server, Access or
account identity changes. Cache/session source keys MUST retain no credentials.
The repository MUST reject results and errors received for a superseded source.
Its source snapshot and sign-in/model arguments MUST describe the same request.
Source: accepted 21 Oct 2026 iOS plan, authentication and cache identity boundaries.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;architecture] client-cancellation-detaches
Cancelling an RPC observer MUST cancel its native request and propagate coroutine
cancellation. It MUST NOT implicitly cancel server-owned AI work. Explicit server
task cancellation MUST remain a separate RPC. Network requests MUST have bounded
connect/read/total timeouts and release native connections on every outcome.
Source: accepted 21 Oct 2026 iOS plan, long-running AI suspension and recovery.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] client-errors-identify-recovery
An HTML response, account/session rejection, forbidden RPC response, non-RPC HTTP
failure, redirect, malformed envelope and server-declared RPC error MUST remain
distinguishable. HTML alone MUST NOT be presented as proof of account expiry or a
specific proxy/login cause. Only a redirect to the fixed HTTPS Cloudflare Access
login origin/path MAY be identified as Access authorization. Failure diagnostics
MUST retain status and bounded response-format categories without raw pages,
redirect URLs, native exception messages or reflected credentials.
Missing or explicit-null results MUST retain the existing null result behavior.
A genuine account-sign-in RPC 429 MUST retain fixed client-owned wait guidance for
the backend's password lockout, without displaying the server's credential-bearing
message. An HTML or non-RPC HTTP 429 MUST retain its actual response category instead.
Source: 21 Oct 2026 first-run Compound review and the existing password throttle.
Source: accepted 21 Oct 2026 iOS plan, API parity and recoverable service access;
Tavi's 21 Oct reinstall screenshot and request for clear first-run actions.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] client-account-discovery-requires-evidence
Account discovery MUST accept only a boolean hasAccount and an optional nonempty
string Google client ID. Malformed account-me results MUST NOT become an expired
session. Connection checks MUST retain an established account when verification
receives HTML, non-RPC HTTP failure, an unavailable server or invalid account data;
an actual RPC session rejection or a different verified email MAY retire it.
An older server's successful Pully response MAY prove connectivity, without
inventing account capabilities. A source change MUST invalidate the whole check.
Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 reinstall screenshot and clear first-run guidance request.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] client-native-integration-is-real
The explicit Darwin integration run MUST exercise the production NSURLSession
transport against a nonprivate loopback fixture, including redirect refusal,
