is absent; ordinary common tests MUST remain usable without that fixture. Source:
Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 iOS implementation request and accepted native-adapter test plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] sign-in-belongs-to-its-opening-source
A sign-in attempt MUST remain bound to the server, Access/account source and UI owner
that opened it. After native account selection and before accepting a server reply,
the controller MUST reject an obsolete owner/source; an old Google token MUST NOT be
sent to a newly configured server. Dismissing native Google selection MUST perform no
sign-in RPC or account commit. A successful synchronous commit MAY advance the source.
Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 maximum-reuse iOS plan and the existing account/source reset
security boundary, preserving settings-sign-in-page's cancellation behavior.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] native-usage-queue-is-owned-and-cancellable
Native usage events MUST retain the existing bounded NDJSON queue, 200-event batch,
refusal/retry and thirty-minute session rules. Loading durable events MUST merge once
with events recorded during startup. A batch acknowledgement MUST NOT remove newer
events, and source retirement or opting out MUST cancel the actual suspended upload.
Native queue files MUST use opaque server/eligible-account/Access namespaces; an old
writer MUST NOT replace a newer source's queue. Queue-file work MUST run on one serial
native worker, and opting out MUST invalidate pending writes before removing the files.
Source: root analytics-can-be-turned-off, analytics-what-not-how-much and Tavi's
21 Oct 2026 full same-app iOS implementation request.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] native-usage-excludes-public-and-unverified-time
Native private usage MUST use the shared PrivateUsageClock policy and require the
current connection's verified foreground authority. Public browsing and time spent
awaiting verification MUST NOT enter private screen or foreground durations. Leaving
that authority MUST settle the previous interval into its existing source queue and
cancel uploads before source replacement; public entry MUST preserve consent and
durable unsent events. Entering private mode after public startup MUST NOT report
public startup/time as a cold private launch. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 independent
Guest decision and the accepted 22 Oct 2026 native usage ownership review.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] client-review-confirmations-send-their-expected-pending-review
When supplied, a drawn review expectation MUST reach Submit or Discard as
pendingReviewId, with explicit null for expected-none. Omitted expectations MUST
retain older callers' wire behavior. Submit's optional drawn head MUST reach the
existing headSha check. Source: the accepted 21 Oct same-app iOS review plan's
current-head and drawn confirmation ownership requirements.
@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] task-cancel-success-is-explicit
A caller which announces that a task stopped MUST request confirmed cancellation
and receive an actual successful RPC response before announcing it. Existing
best-effort cleanup MAY continue to suppress noncancellation failures. Coroutine
cancellation MUST always propagate. Source: Tavi's accepted 21 Oct 2026 complete
native AI journey and the actual held/error Stop regression of 22 Oct 2026.
@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] anonymous-native-browsing-is-independent
Anonymous Popular, repository search and PR lists MUST use only fixed HTTPS
api.github.com REST GETs, with no configured Pully server, Access headers, personal
GitHub credential, session, private cache or AI authority. The shared client MUST
check public repository visibility before requesting its PRs, strictly validate public
data, bound queries/pages/bodies/time, refuse redirects and keep error text fixed.
Opening/paginating a selected repository MUST retain its immutable numeric ID; a name
reused by another repository MUST NOT replace that selected authority or append its PRs.
Native PR visibility/read transactions MUST be serialized within their public client
with a total deadline, so a confirmed denial cannot be undone by an older response.
All public HTTP concurrency MUST remain bounded; no private cache is used as a fallback.
Retired guest sources MUST reject late results/errors and retained callbacks; caller
cancellation MUST close the active native request. HTTP quota metadata MAY contain
only parsed nonnegative numbers. Ordinary RPC POST semantics and their larger diff
budget MUST remain the default. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 signed-out public browsing
request and the approved direct-native guest implementation, independent of ingress.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] personal-sign-in-proof-is-native-and-ephemeral
The personal GitHub sign-in ownership proof MUST encode 32 native CSPRNG bytes as
canonical unpadded base64url. Its challenge MUST be unpadded base64url SHA256 over
the ASCII proof, separate from the backend's OAuth state and PKCE. Proofs MUST NOT
appear in browser URLs, diagnostics, persisted settings or ordinary usage events.
Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 personal GitHub request and the accepted personal-auth
native protocol; backend personal_auth/wire.rs RFC7636 fixture.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] personal-auth-client-has-separate-authority
Personal account requests MUST use only the fixed personal-auth routes of a trusted
HTTPS origin, separate from legacy server configuration. The native adapter MUST NOT
inherit legacy Access headers, cookies, authenticators or shared HTTP caches. Only
personal session/read routes and the explicit repository-consent start MAY send a validated Pully bearer; ownership proofs MUST be
sent only in status/claim/cancel JSON bodies. GitHub credentials MUST remain on the
server. The browser URL MUST use fixed HTTPS GitHub authorization, the captured Pully
callback and S256, or be exactly https://github.com/login/device with a short
upper-case user code that the sheet shows and copies before opening GitHub (GitHub CLI
device sign-in, Tavi, 23 Oct 2026 13:36: "What I want is what you get when you use GH auth login, which is access to all those things regardless of the org permissions."). Normal Connect GitHub MUST request repository consent in the same authorization through
the fixed connect/start route, and require privateRepositories in its claim and confirmation
(Tavi, 25 Oct 2026, one normal login including private repositories). The legacy public
start retains publicRead compatibility. Upgrading an existing public connection MUST
capture the verified initiating account/session and
request only the fixed repository grant (repo/offline_access, or repo read:org for
device sign-in). Source changes/cancellation MUST reject late
results; retired cleanup MAY contact only the captured origin with its own cancelled
attempt/session. HTTP and parse errors MUST retain fixed safe categories, and HTML
or generic HTTP401 MUST NOT imply session expiry. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 personal
GitHub request and the accepted personal_auth native/security boundary.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] personal-sign-in-controller-owns-its-attempt
The native UI owner MUST invoke personal sign-in actions and lifecycle changes on
its UI dispatcher. Each attempt MUST retain its opening origin/source and native
proof only in memory. Normal browser background MUST pause polling while retaining
the same attempt; a bounded one-use claim already in progress MAY finish in that
background. Cancellation, source/route retirement or the bounded deadline MUST
clear pending authority synchronously and reject late browser/result/commit work.
The controller MUST consume a successful claim before publishing its new session
or source, so retirement cannot cancel that accepted session. The claim's original
attempt deadline MUST bound its provisional session. Before bearer GET/session
confirms delivery, the host MUST securely stage the bearer in a separate pending
record; that record MUST NOT restore a principal on process restart. Confirmation
MUST retain the same immutable account/GitHub identity and application authority.
Only the confirmed session MAY be atomically promoted and published. A failed native
stage, confirmation or commit MUST sign out that captured session; local pending
credentials MUST be removed only after confirmed revocation. An uncertain revocation
MUST retain a cleanup-only secure record, never an accepted account. The staging and
cleanup ports MUST use the same UI dispatcher and preserve other accepted accounts.
Explicit cancellation uses
only the captured origin/proof; it MUST NOT alter a legitimate returning legacy
account. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 personal GitHub request and accepted backend
personal_auth native ownership/one-use-claim contract.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] personal-secure-vault-keeps-recovery-separate
The native personal vault MUST atomically persist pending and accepted Pully sessions
through the host's encrypted secure-storage port. Pending credentials MUST NOT restore
a principal after process death. Active in-process confirmation stages MUST be excluded
from unrelated recovery cleanup; losing their owner MUST release that recovery authority.
Promotion MUST match a staged origin, bearer, immutable account/GitHub subject and
application authority. Native records without an authority marker MUST remain publicRead;
a stored publicRead maximum MUST NOT restore privateRepositories authority. A
replaced or locally signed-out accepted session MUST enter a bounded durable revocation
queue, and MUST remain there until captured-origin server sign-out succeeds. Queue
overflow or unavailable secure storage MUST fail closed without dropping another account
or a recovery credential. Only verified matching account status within the securely
stored session's maximum authority MAY become a
visible personal profile; HTML or temporary unavailability MUST preserve saved credentials.
Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 personal GitHub request, accepted backend claim-delivery lease
repair and the 22 Oct native secure-stage/confirm/publish plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] personal-reads-keep-verified-account-authority
A personal read client MUST be issued only from a currently verified personal profile
and its matching accepted secure-vault session. Pending or merely saved credentials
MUST NOT issue it. Every request and result MUST retain the captured origin, session,
account/GitHub subject and current native entry; a changed vault or retired entry MUST
reject late data and errors. Typed personal readers MUST carry that Pully bearer only on their fixed personal GET routes,
with no legacy/Access/cookie authority or GitHub API fallback. Every successful envelope
MUST match the captured immutable account/GitHub identity and the route's explicit
application authority. Public-only reads MUST retain publicRead envelopes and exclude
private data, even for an upgraded account. Account/private reads MUST require the
confirmed privateRepositories session, use only the account route family,
and require explicit repository visibility. Selected repository reads MUST retain
their numeric repository ID and visibility. HTTP concurrency,
body, page and total deadlines MUST remain bounded. Only a valid typed service error
MAY identify session rejection; HTML or a generic HTTP401 MUST NOT expire the account.
Account/capability retirement MUST synchronously clear registered page owners before
another identity can publish data. This GitHub read capability MUST NOT gate independent
default/provider AI. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct any-account/public browsing request,
22 Oct explicit access to the user's private repositories,
and the accepted 22 Oct isolated personal read protocol.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] personal-rejection-revokes-before-secure-cleanup
A current typed account/session rejection from restoration or a personal read MUST
synchronously revoke verified authority, visible profile and every registered read
owner before attempting fallible secure-vault retirement. A failed retirement MUST
preserve the durable credential for recovery, without issuing old or new read handles
until fresh matching verification. A rejection received for a superseded origin,
bearer, verification or native source MUST NOT revoke its replacement. The source-owned
account-recovery action MUST run only after the purge and only while that rejection
still owns the source; HTML and generic HTTP401 MUST retain connection retry instead.
Source: the five independently confirmed 22 Oct 2026 personal-read Compound findings
and Tavi's any-account/private-repository and actionable first-run requirements.
@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] personal-entry-storage-probe-is-not-authority
A personal-entry secure-storage probe MUST read the actual native blob even when the
vault has cached a prior successful read. Missing data MUST remain distinct from a
failed read or present empty/corrupt data, and probe bytes MUST be cleared. Failure
MUST NOT overwrite the vault, make an RPC or authorize browser/claim/read work. The
probe MUST retain the existing vault format/cache and check its current source before
and after native reading; its host MUST supply actual foreground admission before
new account actions. Source: Tavi's 22 Oct 2026 visible native GitHub-entry request
and accepted fixed-intent/secure-admission boundary.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] personal-pr-numbers-fit-native-targets
Personal inventory PR numbers MUST be positive integers within the native target's
signed 32-bit range before publication to shared Inbox rows. An out-of-range number
MUST produce the fixed invalid-response category rather than wrap into another PR.
Source: the shared OpenTarget/PullRow number types and Tavi's 25 Oct 2026 personal Home request.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture;product] github-workspace-is-a-captured-vault-capability
PersonalAccountRuntime MUST issue a full native workspace only after fresh verification
of its accepted vault session with privateRepositories authority. Every workspace RPC
MUST use POST <personal-origin>/workspace/api/rpc with that captured Pully bearer and
the existing name/args and result/error envelope. Sanitized usage batches MUST use
POST <personal-origin>/workspace/api/events with the same captured authority. It MUST NOT copy or mint a legacy
session, use legacy Account preferences or inherit a configured server's credentials.
Source/account replacement, sign-out and actual background admission loss MUST revoke
captured workspace dispatch and late results before another owner appears. A retired
capability MUST NOT revive. HTML/Access failures MUST NOT be treated as account rejection.
Source: Tavi25Oct2026, full production Home and one GitHub app login, and the settled
workspace wire/secure-vault plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] workspace-presentation-outlives-foreground-transport
A verified private session's presentation owner MUST retain the same account, source and
repository identity across an ordinary foreground pause. It MUST NOT itself authorize
dispatch. Each new request MUST acquire that owner's current foreground workspace;
pausing MUST irrevocably retire the captured transport and reject its late replies,
including after resume. The presentation MUST NOT change bearer or immutable account.
Sign-out, account/session replacement or native source retirement MUST synchronously
retire its registered owners. Source: Tavi's 25 Oct 2026 review-fix batch #2, preserving
same-view forms and provider browser roundtrips without weakening workspace admission.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] workspace-retryable-errors-preserve-session
Workspace JSON error responses with HTTP 503 or 429 MUST preserve the accepted secure
session for a same-bearer retry. HTTP 403 scope denial MUST NOT impersonate sign-out.
An actual current workspace JSON 401 rejection MUST revoke the accepted account; HTML
and Access responses MUST remain connection failures. Source: Tavi's 25 Oct 2026
review-fix batch #3 and the route-to-client retry regression requested by its owner.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;product] sync-reads-what-changed
A screen following the server's change feed MUST read again only what a topic it shows
names, through the methods it already calls, and only for the source it started with.
The first answer only places the phone in the feed; an older server without the feed
ends following at once, and repeated failures end it until the screen next comes to the
front, so the screen keeps what it did before. Held waits are left out of call timings.
Source: Tavi, 28 Oct 2026 ("Go") on the plan in thread "Build a sync engine like
Wholana's", building Zero's design that Omar named (call of 26 Oct 2026, 1:01:29).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;architecture] writes-show-first
A write the phone has already shown MUST go out through the outbox: one at a time, in the
order made, retried on no connection, timeouts, 408, 429, 5xx and answers that are not
the server's own, and dropped only on the server's own 4xx refusal, after which the page
reads the server's state back. A read of the same state MUST lay the unsent writes over
the server's answer, so a write never shows undone before it arrived. A source change
MUST drop every queued write. Source: as sync-reads-what-changed.
